# Painted parts

Recorded from the dog look pass (01.09). The same faults then went
into Crow / Chicken. Do not repeat them.

A species is one animal. Ten separate image calls are ten animals.
Judge the assembled body in Play, not the folder of crops.

## One sheet, then crop

- Draw or generate **one** side-view sheet (face +X), then split.
  A locked reference on every later call is a fallback, not a plan.
- Human already learned this: Yury's `ArtIncoming/Human` sheet, then
  `Tools/SplitSheet`. Do not invent a new pipeline per species.

## One bone per PNG

- The drawing is that segment only. No extra neck on the head, no
  shoulder on the chest, no shin on the paw, no second joint bend
  painted into a straight bone.
- Axis of the art = axis of the collider (horizontal trunk / tail /
  paw; vertical limb). Proximal toward the parent joint.
- Dog `front_upper` had a painted knee on a straight 0.07×0.17 box.
  Dog `pelvis` read as a shoulder. Dog `thigh` read as a human arm.
  That is a wrong crop, not a coefficient.

## Do not Sliced-stretch

`HumanSegment` sets `sprite.size` to `VisualSize(collider)`. That
ignores PNG aspect. Human hands became sausages (collider 0.06×0.32).
Dog tail is 0.20×0.05 (aspect 4) on art ~1.5. Only `Human/hand` is
exempt today.

Before a part ships: PNG aspect vs collider aspect. If they differ by
more than about a quarter, either recrop the art or size the sprite
from the PNG (collider unchanged). Do not "fix" it by changing
`handSize` / `pawSize` / `tailSize`.

## Joints

`VisualSize` grows the sprite so neighbours overlap. A padded PNG
defeats that: `Sliced` maps empty canvas into the box, fur sits in
the middle, sky shows at the hinge (dog chest was ~38% opaque).
Crop to `OpaqueRect` before `Sliced`. Painted overlap along the bone
is 1.36, not 1.18. Do not close a gap by moving the collider.

A hard outline on the cut face becomes a dark seam when two bones
rotate. Leave the cut soft. Do not bake a posed bend that fights
the hinge.

## Background

Transparent. Punch only near-white, low chroma. A black studio fill
stays as an opaque slab. Check corner **and** a pixel beside the
silhouette, not only `A00=0`.

## Done means assembled

Crops in `ArtIncoming/*/gen` are not acceptance. Open the Play scene
of that species (`Dog`, `Bird`, `Chicken`). If Unity is closed, say
so — do not call the folder "the dog".
